  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SC 1 - Mitigating the Impact of Typhoons on Vulnerable Populations in Bicol and Eastern Visayas Regions through CCCM and Shelter Anticipatory Actions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The key objective of the project is to mitigate the physical and socioeconomic harm induced by sudden evacuation of the most vulnerable population affected by typhoons in Bicol region and Eastern Visayas region. The project focuses on families living in houses made of light materials less durable to typhoons and in hazard-prone zones. It augments the local government&#x2019;s life-saving measures in response to disasters, namely the mandatory pre-emptive evacuation, which these vulnerable families will most likely be subject to at the time of destructive typhoons. Through this project, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) ensures that internally displaced persons have access to safe and dignified living conditions at evacuation centres at the onset of their pre-emptive evacuation. Through cash-based interventions, IOM is also facilitating immediate access to appropriate materials and tools for internally displaced persons to repair their shelters right after typhoons&apos; landfall.</narrative>
  </description>
